%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: a2.2 Morning care - stakeholders
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Stakeholders ST-08 to ST-12 for the morning personal care routine (tooth brushing and medication support). This material is unrelated to the main concept of social introductions (see [[a2.1 Residents, family and staff>>doc:1 Foundation.a2 Stakeholders.a2\.1 Residents, family and staff.WebHome]]). IDs continue after the main set.

= Stakeholder - Resident with dementia [ST-08] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-08
|Name|Resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-05 to SA-07. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Direct - interacts with the System during the activity
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-10: Dignity (high)

- HV-09: Autonomy (high)

- HV-13: Well-being (high)

- HV-12: Competence (medium)

- HV-11: Privacy (medium)
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Receives day-to-day support from ST-09 care workers. ST-10 family members may visit and be involved in care decisions, including consent. Receives medical care from ST-12, and lives in a home run by ST-11.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-05, SA-06; holds → HV-09, HV-10, HV-11, HV-12, HV-13; appears-in → PS-05, PS-06; elaborated-as → HP-04 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Care home staff member [ST-09] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-09
|Name|Care home staff member
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-05 to SA-07. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Direct - receives handover requests and reviews the session record
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-13: Well-being (high)

- HV-14: Attentive care (high)

- HV-10: Dignity (medium)

- HV-09: Autonomy (medium) - endorses it for residents, but weighs it against the time available

- HV-12: Competence (medium)

- HV-11: Privacy (medium) - for residents, and against surveillance of their own work
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Supports several ST-08 residents per shift. Employed by ST-11. Keeps ST-10 informed about their relative, and coordinates with ST-12 on medication and health.

== Graph edges ==

performs → SA-07; supports → SA-05, SA-06; holds → HV-09 to HV-14; appears-in → PS-05, PS-06; elaborated-as → HP-05 (§2.2).

= Stakeholder - Family members of Resident [ST-10] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-10
|Name|Family members of Resident
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-05 to SA-07. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - affected by outcomes, does not interact with the System and does not receive its records
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-13: Well-being (high)

- HV-10: Dignity (high)

- HV-09: Autonomy (medium)

- HV-14: Attentive care (medium)

- HV-11: Privacy (low) - may want more information about their relative than the resident would choose to share
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Relatives of ST-08. In contact with ST-09 about their relative's care, and may be involved in consent decisions on ST-08's behalf.

== Graph edges ==

holds → HV-09, HV-10, HV-11, HV-13, HV-14.

= Stakeholder - Management or the Owners of the care home [ST-11] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-11
|Name|Management or the Owners of the care home
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-05 to SA-07. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - decides on adopting the System, does not interact with it
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-14: Attentive care (high) - staffing and workload

- HV-13: Well-being (high) - quality of care

- HV-11: Privacy (medium) - data-protection obligations for residents and staff

- HV-10: Dignity (medium)
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Employs ST-09. Responsible for the home's quality of care, staffing and data protection, and for the living environment of ST-08.

== Graph edges ==

holds → HV-10, HV-11, HV-13, HV-14.

= Stakeholder - Medical staff: GP, Nurse [ST-12] =

//Who is affected. In the Foundation, captured by exactly two things: the values they hold, and their relationship to other Stakeholders. A full behavioral Persona is built later, in the Specification, for Direct Stakeholders only.//

**Report Format:** §1.1 Operational Demands

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|ST-12
|Name|Medical staff: GP, Nurse
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. The stakeholder set is derived from SA-05 to SA-07. Values and priorities are the group's reasoning.
|Type|Indirect - responsible for care plans and medication, does not interact with the System
|Values and motivations|(((
- HV-13: Well-being (high)

- HV-11: Privacy (medium) - medical confidentiality

- HV-09: Autonomy (medium)
)))
|Relationship to other Stakeholders|Prescribes and reviews ST-08's medication and health. Relies on ST-09 to carry out care plans day to day.

== Graph edges ==

